# ============================================================
# Outbound HTTP/1.1 client (fetcher suite)
# ============================================================
# Lets a SemanticScript app call another service over HTTP. The native runtime
# owns only the minimal socket primitive (ss_http_client_fetch); these wrappers
# provide the typed, ergonomic GET/POST surface. Returned bodies are heap-owned
# by the caller (free via c.free) and are null on transport error or non-2xx.

# rationale: clientGet fixes the HTTP method to GET. Pass an empty
#   headerLine when no extra single-line header is needed.
# memory: returned non-null body is heap-owned by caller and must be released with c.free.
# failure: returns null on connection failure, malformed response, timeout in the native adapter, or non-2xx status.
operation clientGet
input operation clientGet host String
input operation clientGet port Int32
input operation clientGet path String
input operation clientGet headerLine String
output operation clientGet HttpClientResponseBody
effect clientGet read http.client
memory clientGet heap yes
async clientGet no
useCapability clientGet httpClientCaller
purpose operation clientGet "Issue a blocking HTTP GET to host:port path with an optional header line; return the response body on 2xx, else null."
label startClientGet
call clientGetCall clientFetchNative
argument clientGetCall method String httpClientMethodGet
argument clientGetCall host String host
argument clientGetCall port Int32 port
argument clientGetCall path String path
argument clientGetCall headerLine String headerLine
argument clientGetCall body String httpClientEmptyBody
run clientGetCall
bind value clientGetBody HttpClientResponseBody clientGetCall
return value clientGetBody

# rationale: clientPost fixes the HTTP method to POST. body is sent as
#   the request body and headerLine carries one optional caller-supplied
#   header.
# memory: returned non-null body is heap-owned by caller and must be released with c.free.
# failure: returns null on connection failure, malformed response, timeout in the native adapter, or non-2xx status.
operation clientPost
input operation clientPost host String
input operation clientPost port Int32
input operation clientPost path String
input operation clientPost headerLine String
input operation clientPost body String
output operation clientPost HttpClientResponseBody
effect clientPost read http.client
memory clientPost heap yes
async clientPost no
useCapability clientPost httpClientCaller
purpose operation clientPost "Issue a blocking HTTP POST (JSON body) to host:port path with an optional header line; return the response body on 2xx, else null."
label startClientPost
call clientPostCall clientFetchNative
argument clientPostCall method String httpClientMethodPost
argument clientPostCall host String host
argument clientPostCall port Int32 port
argument clientPostCall path String path
argument clientPostCall headerLine String headerLine
argument clientPostCall body String body
run clientPostCall
bind value clientPostBody HttpClientResponseBody clientPostCall
return value clientPostBody

# rationale: Low-level runtimeBinding hook used by standard.http clientGet/clientPost.
operation clientFetchNative
input operation clientFetchNative method String
input operation clientFetchNative host String
input operation clientFetchNative port Int32
input operation clientFetchNative path String
input operation clientFetchNative headerLine String
input operation clientFetchNative body String
output operation clientFetchNative HttpClientResponseBody
effect clientFetchNative read http.client
memory clientFetchNative heap yes
async clientFetchNative no
useCapability clientFetchNative httpClientCaller
operationBody clientFetchNative runtimeBinding
purpose operation clientFetchNative "Low-level runtimeBinding hook used by standard.http clientGet/clientPost."
runtimeBindingPrecondition clientFetchNative "method/host/path are non-null; returns a heap-owned 2xx response body or null."
runtimeBinding clientFetchNative native.ss_http_client_fetch

# rationale: use escapeHtml before reflecting untrusted text into
#   htmlContentType responses.
# memory: scratch is caller-owned writable memory; capacity must include the trailing NUL byte.
# failure: output is bounded by capacity; callers that need lossless output must size scratch for worst-case escaping.
operation escapeHtml
input operation escapeHtml input String
input operation escapeHtml scratch OpaquePointer
input operation escapeHtml capacity Int32
output operation escapeHtml String
effect escapeHtml readWrite memory.buffer
memory escapeHtml arena request
async escapeHtml no
useCapability escapeHtml httpEscapeBufferWriter
operationBody escapeHtml runtimeBinding
purpose operation escapeHtml "Escape HTML special characters (& < > \" ') from input into the caller-provided scratch buffer; returns the bounded, null-terminated escaped string."
runtimeBindingPrecondition escapeHtml "scratch points to at least capacity writable bytes; input is non-null."
runtimeBinding escapeHtml native.ss_http_html_escape
